    "['delete set protocols bgp group [group_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'no neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'no neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper delete commands to Cisco equivalent commands:\\n\\n##\\nno neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate\\nno bgp redistribute-internal\\nno synchronization\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The \"activate\" command removal translates directly to Cisco\\'s \"no neighbor activate\" command\\n2. The \"redistribute connected\" removal translates to \"no bgp redistribute-internal\" in Cisco\\n3. The \"no synchronization\" removal translates to simply enabling synchronization with \"no synchronization\" in Cisco\\n\\nNote: The first Juniper command \"delete set protocols bgp group external local-address 30.30.30.30\" doesn\\'t have a direct Cisco equivalent in this context since it\\'s removing an IPv4 address that wasn\\'t actually configured in the Cisco context (which is already using IPv6).', 'trans_template': 'no neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'no bgp redistribute-internal', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'no bgp redistribute-internal', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper delete commands to Cisco equivalent commands:\\n\\n##\\nno neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate\\nno bgp redistribute-internal\\nno synchronization\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The \"activate\" command removal translates directly to Cisco\\'s \"no neighbor activate\" command\\n2. The \"redistribute connected\" removal translates to \"no bgp redistribute-internal\" in Cisco\\n3. The \"no synchronization\" removal translates to simply enabling synchronization with \"no synchronization\" in Cisco\\n\\nNote: The first Juniper command \"delete set protocols bgp group external local-address 30.30.30.30\" doesn\\'t have a direct Cisco equivalent in this context since it\\'s removing an IPv4 address that wasn\\'t actually configured in the Cisco context (which is already using IPv6).', 'trans_template': 'no bgp redistribute-internal'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'no synchronization', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper delete commands to Cisco equivalent commands:\\n\\n##\\nno neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate\\nno bgp redistribute-internal\\nno synchronization\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The \"activate\" command removal translates directly to Cisco\\'s \"no neighbor activate\" command\\n2. The \"redistribute connected\" removal translates to \"no bgp redistribute-internal\" in Cisco\\n3. The \"no synchronization\" removal translates to simply enabling synchronization with \"no synchronization\" in Cisco\\n\\nNote: The first Juniper command \"delete set protocols bgp group external local-address 30.30.30.30\" doesn\\'t have a direct Cisco equivalent in this context since it\\'s removing an IPv4 address that wasn\\'t actually configured in the Cisco context (which is already using IPv6).', 'trans_template': 'no synchronization'}]]": 1,
    "['local-address [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'no neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 update-source 30.30.30.30', 'parent_command': ['no neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate'], 'root': 'no neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nno neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 update-source 30.30.30.30\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command removes the IPv4 local-address (30.30.30.30) for BGP peering\\n- In Cisco, this would be equivalent to removing the IPv4 update-source for the neighbor\\n- Since the neighbor is specified as IPv6 (2001:db8:2::2), we reference that in the Cisco command\\n- The \"no\" prefix is used to remove the configuration in Cisco IOS\\n- Note that Cisco doesn\\'t have separate group/external hierarchy like Juniper, so we directly reference the neighbor', 'trans_template': 'no neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 update-source 30.30.30.30'}]]": 1,
