    "['term [parameter2] from protocol [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map EXPORT-CONNECTED permit 10', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 100'], 'root': 'router bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map EXPORT-CONNECTED permit 10\\n match interface *\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `from protocol direct` matches directly connected routes\\n- In Cisco, the equivalent is `match interface *` which matches all directly connected interfaces\\n- The `term 1` in Juniper translates to sequence number `10` in Cisco's route-map\\n- The `then accept` is implied by the `permit` action in the route-map\", 'trans_template': 'route-map EXPORT-CONNECTED permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match interface *', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 100'], 'root': 'router bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map EXPORT-CONNECTED permit 10\\n match interface *\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `from protocol direct` matches directly connected routes\\n- In Cisco, the equivalent is `match interface *` which matches all directly connected interfaces\\n- The `term 1` in Juniper translates to sequence number `10` in Cisco's route-map\\n- The `then accept` is implied by the `permit` action in the route-map\", 'trans_template': 'match interface *'}]]": 1,
